[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines, and its page says: one issue, one fix
queued. The reports say otherwise. Read by tenant, booking form and channel, and with the body of
each report read, the ticket holds three problems. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix does not close #4471. It fixes the parser problem only. The other two stay
open until they get their own fixes.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

### `parser` · the shared parser reads every date month first

A day-first tenant writes the 7th of April as 07/04. The shared parser reads it as 4 July. The
report shows the same two numbers, swapped: "Our 7 April reminder went out on 4 July." It reaches
every day-first tenant through the app, email and the booking-v2 form. Ticket
[#1](https://github.com/shawky84/mega-support-kb/issues/1).

### `hint` · booking-v3 tells people to type the month first

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so people type the month first, as
told. The form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The report looks the same as a
parser report, so reading it does not tell them apart: only the tenant's form and the `form`
channel do. The parser fix does not touch this one. The fix is the hint, or how the form reads
it. Ticket [#2](https://github.com/shawky84/mega-support-kb/issues/2).

### `one-day` · the date moves by one day

These reports show no swap. A Tuesday turns into a Monday. A client in Lisbon gets Tuesday and a
client in Toronto gets Monday for the same meeting. An invite arrives before the booking was
made. The date shifts by one day, the way a time-zone or midnight conversion shifts it. The desk
noted these reports in `desk-notes.json` but counted them under `parser` by tenant. Ticket
[#3](https://github.com/shawky84/mega-support-kb/issues/3).

## How the split was made

- **One id, one report.** The export repeats some reports across its pages. Duplicates are dropped.
- **Cause by tenant, not by intake.** The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It
  disagrees with the tenant in both the `parser` and the `hint` groups.
- **Bodies read, not only subjects.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
  merges on the subject alone. Most subjects in #4471 appear under more than one problem, so the
  subject cannot tell the problems apart.

## For the desk

- Stop merging new date reports into #4471 by subject. Route them by tenant locale, booking form
  and channel (`causes.ts`), and read the body for a one-day move.
- Decision 0001 is past its review date. A new record should replace it.

